{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791369169,"nonce":"1U1+Rz5Vp5bPjV4eue+7tgeK2iQ=","title":"Dynamic numeric result inference is conflated with erased concrete arithmetic","message":"Native Haxe Context.typeof reports Float for d - 1, d * 2, d / 2 and d % 3 when d is explicitly Dynamic. Rayzor currently reports Dynamic for those expressions. Probe: /tmp/rayzor-nullable-arithmetic/UnaryTypes.hx; haxe-conformance/regressions/BoxedNumericOperators.hx checks the numeric payload and concrete call boundaries, without claiming these binary inferred types are fixed.\n\nSimply returning Float whenever either operand is typed Dynamic is unsafe with the current lowering: unannotated abstract methods returning this and some standard-library concrete operations also decay to Dynamic. Coercing all such arithmetic to Float changes integer overflow and erased argument/return representations. Full rejected v5 run /tmp/rayzor-nullable-unary-final-v5/report.tsv lost seven baseline passes, including Issue2661 and Issue3806 (Float bit patterns read as Int), Issue5090 (SHA-1), and XML rows. ConcreteArithmeticResults.hx and PostfixLoopsIterables.hx failed as well.\n\nRecover concrete operand/return types or distinguish genuinely boxed Dynamic expressions before changing numeric result inference. Preserve Int overflow in cryptographic code and Int-backed abstracts. Current boxed numeric operator work narrows the fix to payload operations and Dynamic-to-concrete numeric method argument conversions.","files":null}]}